# Talent Perak 2.0 - Hono API rules

## Stack
- Hono + `@hono/zod-openapi` + Drizzle PostgreSQL.
- Better Auth via `drizzleAdapter` (never a raw `pool` as `database`).
- Auth HTTP is only `app.all("/api/auth/*", (c) => auth.handler(c.req.raw))`.

## Auth plugins
Enable: `admin`, `organization` (with `ac` Role objects, not string arrays), `customSession`, `bearer`, `openAPI`, `i18n` (`@better-auth/i18n`, locales `en` | `ms`), optional `genericOAuth` (MyDigital ID).
Do NOT add `user.additionalFields.role` — the admin plugin owns `user.role`.
Do NOT add a static `support` role. Company roles are created with `organization.createRole`; platform roles are rows in `platform_role`.
`createAccessControl` is a helper, not a plugin.

## Access control
- `src/auth/access/catalog.ts` is the single source of truth: each resource lists only the actions its routes support. Both `platformAc` and `organizationAc` are built from it.
- Guard routes with `requirePermission(resource, action)`, `requireCompanyPermission`, `requireTvetPermission`, or `requirePermissionFor` when the action depends on the payload. Never branch on role names.

## Layout
- `src/auth/`: instance, middleware, plugins, access catalogs.
- `src/db/`: connection, schema barrel, relations, migrations. No feature dumps.
- `src/features/<name>/`: `*.route.ts`, `*.controller.ts`, `*.service.ts`, `*.repository.ts`, `validator/`.

## SRS
- New orgs: `status` default `PENDING_APPROVAL`. Use `requireApprovedCompany` or `requireCompanyPermission` on vacancy/applicant writes.
- Vacancies (Phase 4+): start `PENDING_APPROVAL`.
- TVET: `hasTvetCapability`, not a separate account type.
- CORS + `trustedOrigins` must include `FRONTEND_URL` with `credentials: true`.
